{
  "assessment": "The source packet provides a complete quantitative description of the quasi-2D XY model with a V plane intersected by P planes. The selected cluster focuses on the long-range ordered phase for K >= K2, with four parameter sets P1-P4. The controls are the coupling strengths W and K, and the readouts are the large-distance spin-spin correlation G_y and the magnetic fluctuations <M^2_y> along the y-direction. The mechanism is the Goldstone-mode power-law decay with exponent q, and the claims encode the FSS relations G_y = a + b L^{-q} and <M^2_y> = a + b L^{-q}. The source provides explicit numeric values for q, a, b, and their uncertainties for each parameter set, along with fit statistics. The case is authoring-ready because there are numeric controls (W, K), a numeric readout (G_y, <M^2_y>), a quantitative mechanism (Goldstone-mode decay), and an objective source-grounded response within an explicit domain (K >= K2).",
